  "instruction": "Using Visual Studio Code, create a new Python script called glucose_bmi_viz.py in the /home/user/analysis_results/ directory. Load the dataset diabetes.csv (already available in that folder). Then create two visualizations: (1) `glucose_bmi_scatter.png` — a scatter plot of Glucose vs BMI, color-coded by Outcome; (2) `glucose_hist.png` — a histogram comparing Glucose distributions for diabetic (Outcome = 1) and non-diabetic (Outcome = 0) individuals. Ensure both charts include clear titles, axis labels, and a legend where appropriate.Finally, create a single slide in Microsoft PowerPoint that includes both visualizations and clearly communicates the key insights and overall story shown by the charts.",
  "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/plotly/datasets/refs/heads/master/diabetes.csv",
